r fabrication shop delivers precision-crafted components built to exact specifications", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Service-disabled veteran-owned", "Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dk-fabrication-and-welding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Drapery Manufacturing Inc., doing business as DMI Wholesale Textile, was founded in 1975 in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. The company operates a 32,000-square-foot manufacturing facility centrally located in the United States, allowing it to service customers nationwide.

The company custom manufactures draperies, curtains, bedding, and window-treatment hardware for hospitality, multi-housing, commercial, and healthcare markets. Its turnkey service includes professional field measuring, manufacturing, and installation. Capabilities cover hospitality drapes, multi-housing window coverings, commercial and office draperies, hospital cubicle and privacy curtains, food-service curtains, grommet draperies, valances, cornices, Roman and flat-fold shades, solar shades, wood blinds, and a range of hardware such as Graber tracks, wrought-iron rods, and cubicle track systems. DMI also offers COM (customer’s own material) labor and sources fabrics from major suppliers.

Primary customers include interior designers, decorators, hotel and motel operators, university and apartment housing managers, healthcare facility administrators, nursing homes, clinics, and food-service establishments. The firm has supplied window coverings for hotel renovations, university dormitories, hospital privacy curtains, and restaurant kitchen partitions.

DMI emphasizes its 1975 founding, a solid Dun & Bradstreet credit history, and a commitment to never delaying a grand opening. It sells wholesale to the trade only, offers competitive pricing, and ensures all custom draperies are tabled for size with lined top-treatment boards. Flame-retardant hospital curtains meet NFPA 701 standards, and the company can supply any fabric or work with customer-provided material.', certifications=ARRAY['NFPA 701']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom drapery manufacturing", "Field measuring", "Installation", "COM (customer''s own material) labor", "Turnkey project management", "Wholesale manufacturing", "Fabric sourcing", "Hardware supply (tracks, rods, blinds, shades)", "Hospital cubicle curtain manufacturing", "Privacy curtain manufacturing", "Flame-retardant treatment (NFPA 701)", "Antibacterial curtain manufacturing", "Disposable fabric curtain manufacturing", "Food-service curtain manufacturing", "Valance and cornice fabrication", "Roman and flat-fold shade fabrication", "Grommet drapery fabrication", "Cut yardage service", "Bedding manufacturing", "Solar shade fabrication", "Wood blind fabrication", "Wrought iron rod fabrication", "Cubicle track system installation", "Graber hardware installation"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Multi-housing (apartments, university housing)", "Commercial (offices, facilities)", "Healthcare (hospitals, nursing homes, clinics, dental)", "Food-service (restaurants, kitchens)"], "materials": ["Fabric (various)", "Customer''s Own Material (COM)", "Disposable fabric", "Flame-retardant fabric (NFPA 701)", "Antibacterial fabric", "Sterile fabric"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Turnkey service: field measuring, manufacturing, and installation", "32,000 sq ft manufacturing facility centrally located in Oklahoma City", "Wholesale to trade only with competitive pricing", "NFPA 701 compliant flame-retardant hospital curtains", "COM (customer''s own material) labor available"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 -> db", "Headquarters Oklahoma City, Oklahoma -> db", "32,000 sq ft manufacturing facility -> /about", "Turnkey service including field measuring, manufacturing, installation -> /", "Wholesale to trade only -> /about", "Competitive pricing -> /about", "Custom draperies tabled for size -> /about", "Top treatment boards covered with lining -> /about", "Never delay a grand opening -> /about", "COM labor offered -> /, /about", "Fabrics sourced from major suppliers -> /", "Hospitality drapery manufacturing -> /", "Multi-housing window coverings for apartments and university housing -> /", "Commercial draperies for offices and healthcare facilities -> /", "Hospital cubicle and privacy curtains -> /", "Food-service curtains for restaurants and kitchens -> /", "NFPA 701 flame-retardant compliance -> /", "Antibacterial curtains -> /", "Disposable fabric curtains -> /", "Hardware supply (Graber, wrought iron, solar shades, wood blinds) -> /", "Valances, cornices, Roman shades, flat-fold shades, grommet draperies, cut yardage -> /", "Bedding manufacturing -> /", "Centrally located for nationwide service -> /", "Dun & Bradstreet credit history -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a national wholesale manufacturer of hospitality drapery, multi-housing and commercial draperies and bedding.", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='dmi-wholesale-textile' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DN Plastics was founded in 1998 in Morrison, Tennessee, as a family-owned business. The company is certified as a Women-Owned Minority Business Enterprise.

The company manufactures engineered thermoplastic compounds, sheets, and gels, operating six compounding lines — four Coperion 70 mm twin-screw and two single-screw extruders — with a combined capacity exceeding 100 million pounds per year. Its 120,000-square-foot facility includes a sheet extrusion line capable of producing up to 90-inch-wide sheet with co-extrusion and lamination capabilities, and is served by rail for bulk logistics. DN Plastics also offers toll compounding, new product development, and analytical testing services from a laboratory equipped with FTIR, DSC, TGA, and DMA instruments.

Its customer base spans automotive and non-automotive sectors. Automotive applications include interior trim components, door panels, cowl-vent grilles, blow-molded air ducts, engine covers, dash insulators, door insulators, flooring insulators, non-carpeted flooring, and cargo van liners. Non-automotive markets served include sporting goods, toys, wire and cable, healthcare products, household appliances, furniture, and general household items.

