UPDATE companies SET description='Daechang Indiana, Inc is headquartered in Indianapolis, Indiana. The company operates as the U.S. presence of Daechang Seat Co., Ltd., a South Korean manufacturer with a 40-year history in automotive seating components. The Korean parent company, Daechang Seat Co., Ltd., is based in Hwaseong, Gyeonggi-do, and presents itself as a specialist in seat frame and mechanism production.

The company produces seat frames, power lumbar supports, suspension assemblies, and rear cushion frames for passenger vehicles. The product portfolio covers front and rear seat frame assemblies, 2-way and 4-way lumbar supports, front back suspension assemblies, rear back frame assemblies, rear cushion frame wire assemblies, and third-row cushion leg assemblies.

Parts are fitted to models such as the Avante (AD), Sonata (LF), i30 (PD), Tucson (TL), i40 (VF), and Genesis (VI). The company also integrates seating technology from German specialist Brose for select applications.

