UPDATE companies SET description='Fairfield Manufacturing operates its primary North American production hub in Lafayette, Indiana. The company traces its origins to 1919, establishing a century-long focus on custom gears and drive systems.

The Lafayette campus spans 60,000 square meters and houses more than 600 machine tools and 60 furnaces, with 7,000 square meters dedicated to heat treatment. In-house capabilities cover the full product lifecycle: engineering and design (including reverse engineering and clean-sheet development), gear cutting (external, internal, high-speed, planetary, hypoid, and Zerol configurations), shaft machining, heat treating (carburizing, annealing, nitriding, induction), precision machining (drilling, milling, tapping, sawing), metallurgical testing, failure analysis, product performance validation in lab and field, and large-scale assembly and inspection. Gear quality is certified to AGMA Class 14.

Global original equipment manufacturers in marine, mining, oil and gas, railway, environment, energy, recycling, and construction equipment (including compact track loaders) rely on Fairfield for integrated gear production. The plant produces Spicer Torque-Hub track drives and other large components such as bull gears, pinions, and starter gears for on- and offshore applications.

Fairfield differentiates itself through fully integrated, in-house control of design, manufacturing, testing, and certification, backed by approvals from the American Bureau of Shipping, Lloyd’s Register, the Association of American Railroads, DNV, and the Performance Review Institute. Its engineering team specializes in resolving gear noise, heat, vibration, and early-failure issues, offering both build-to-print and complete solution services.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','Lloyds Register','Performance Review Institute Transportation and Power Generation Program','DNV','AGMA Class 14 gear quality certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering and design services", "Reverse engineering", "Make-to-print manufacturing", "Complete design, manufacturing, and testing services", "Gear cutting (external, internal, high-speed, planetary, hypoid, Zerol)", "Shaft manufacturing", "Heat treating (carburizing, annealing, nitriding, induction)", "Precision machining (drilling, milling, tapping, sawing)", "Metallurgical testing", "Advanced metallurgy processes", "Failure analysis of gears and assemblies", "Product performance testing (lab and field)", "Large-scale assembly", "Inspection and quality certification (AGMA Class 14)", "Non-destructive testing", "Automated assembly with manufacturing execution system", "Lean manufacturing"], "industries": ["Marine", "Mining", "Oil and gas", "Railway", "Environment", "Energy", "Recycling", "Construction equipment", "Offshore", "Industrial", "Mobile equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["60 furnaces", "600 machine tools", "Multi-tasking machining centers with meter-plus size capabilities", "CNC inspection technology", "Automated assembly lines with manufacturing execution system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully integrated in-house design, manufacturing, testing, and assembly", "Gear quality certified to AGMA Class 14", "Over 60 furnaces and 600 machine tools on 60,00