UPDATE companies SET description='Daniels Manufacturing Corporation (DMC) is headquartered in Orlando, Florida. The company traces its roots to 1947 when founder Bill Daniels began a general job-shop in Pontiac, Michigan, producing components for automotive manufacturers such as Ford. Incorporated in 1949 in Bloomfield Hills, Michigan, DMC is a veteran-owned small business that emphasizes a family culture across its operations.

DMC designs and manufactures precision crimp tools, connector assembly tool kits, wire preparation tools, and specialty products including Safe-T-Cable® and LaceLok® for mission-critical electrical systems. Its in-house manufacturing encompasses CNC milling and turning, electrical discharge machining (EDM), and precision grinding, supporting custom tooling projects from concept through testing. The company operates a state-of-the-art facility with dozens of modern machines and maintains a global distributor network in more than 35 countries; many of its tools appear on the Department of Defense Qualified Product List (QPL).

DMC serves government and defense (ground, naval, aviation, space), commercial aviation (OEM, MRO, eVTOL, rotorcraft, airlines), space (satellites, launch vehicles), medical device manufacturers, telecommunications (military and RF wireless networks), automotive (OEM, motorsport, off-highway), rail (wayside, locomotive), power generation (hydro, solar, wind, nuclear), and automation (mining, robotics).

