UPDATE companies SET description='Diamond Electric Mfg. Corp traces its roots to 1937 when Inosuke Tomita founded Diamond Electric in Japan. The company established its U.S. presence in 1990 with Nobu Hashimoto as the first president of Diamond Electric United States (DEUS). After a groundbreaking ceremony in April 1996 attended by then-Governor Gaston Caperton, the Eleanor, West Virginia plant began mass production of ignition coils in May 1997. The corporate headquarters remains in Eleanor, WV, while a sales and design center operates in Farmington Hills, Michigan, near Detroit’s automotive hub.

The company designs, manufactures, and distributes automotive electrical components, specializing in ignition coils for original equipment manufacturers. Its U.S. operations encompass manufacturing at the Eleanor facility, which has undergone multiple expansions since 1997, and engineering support from the Michigan center. Products are thoroughly tested to meet OEM standards, and the firm emphasizes research as a key step in new product development.

Diamond Electric serves three primary customer segments: global OEM automotive manufacturers, service part retailers, and DIY installers. Its ignition coils are supplied to major automakers, and the company has earned quality and delivery awards from several of them, including a President’s Product Quality Award from Subaru of Indiana Automotive in 2004.

The company’s stated philosophy—“We Are Diverse Shiny Diamonds. We Are Seeking the Happiness of Our Comrades, By Supporting Our Customers First, By Contributing to Society, With the Commitment to Earn Their Trust”—drives a quality policy focused on on-time, defect-free delivery and constant improvement through teamwork. Community involvement is also highlighted, with donations to local parks and schools in Putnam County.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design Engineering", "Research and Development", "Ignition Coil Manufacturing", "Product Testing", "Distribution", "Sales and Technical Support"], "industries": ["Automotive Electrical", "Automotive Ignition Products", "Automotive OEM", "Aftermarket Automotive Parts"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multiple U.S. manufacturing and design locations enabling broad customer support", "Quality policy targeting on-time, defect-free delivery with continuous improvement", "Research-driven design engineering for new product performance", "Recognized with quality awards from major automotive OEMs", "Long-tenured workforce with original team members still employed"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1937 by Inosuke Tomita -> /about", "U.S. operations began 1990, Eleanor WV plant groundbreaking 1996, production 1997 -> /about", "Headquarters in Eleanor, WV; sales/design center in Farmington Hills, MI -> /", "Designs, manufactures, distributes automotive electrical components (ignition coils) -> /", "Multiple U.S. locations provide manufacturing, sales, support for global OEM customers -> /", "Quality policy: on-time, defect-free delivery, constant improvement -> /", "Philosophy: ''We Are Diverse Shiny Diamonds...'' -> /about", "Recognized for quality awards from major automotive manufacturers, e.g., Subaru 2004 -> /about", "Certifications: ISO14001, IATF16949 -> db", "Industries served: automotive electrical, automotive ignition products -> db", "Customer segments: OEM automotive manufacturers, service part retailers, DIY installers -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Diamond Electric designs, manufactures, and distributes automotive electrical components.", "founded_year": "1937", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='diamond-electric-mfg-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Diamond Medical Equipment & Supply operates from a showroom at 300 South Rodney Parham in Little Rock, Arkansas. The company has served the Central Arkansas region for over four decades, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership details and founder names are not stated in available sources.

The business functions as a retail supplier of home medical equipment and supplies, carrying products from manufacturers such as Pride Mobility and Golden Technology. Its showroom — described as the largest in Arkansas — stocks mobility devices including power chairs, scooters, and lift chairs, alongside daily living aids. The company also offers equipment rentals, repair and parts services, and white-glove delivery that includes setup and tutorial within Central Arkansas.

Customers include individuals, caretakers, medical professionals, nursing homes, and assisted living facilities.

