UPDATE companies SET description='Diversified Metal Fabricators operates from Ferndale, Michigan, where it was established in 1993.

The company fabricates custom ductwork, fittings, transitions, plenums, and one-off parts when catalog items do not fit field conditions. It also produces brackets, signs, panels, covers, and other repeatable parts in premium galvanized steel. Processes include cutting, bending, forming, and mechanical joint assembly without exposed fasteners. The shop handles orders ranging from single pieces to production quantities.

Primary customers are HVAC contractors, mechanical contractors, and retrofit crews who need parts that match existing field dimensions. The company also works directly with homeowners requiring custom duct transitions or replacement fittings. Examples include ductwork that will not land on the job, custom carts, and residential retrofit pieces.

Diversified Metal Fabricators emphasizes a streamlined quoting process: customers can send a drawing, photo of a print, marked-up screenshot, hand sketch, or the old part itself. The team offers field measurement assistance and walks through the part before quoting. Finished parts are fabricated to precise specifications and made ready for quick pickup.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["HVAC ductwork fabrication", "Custom sheet metal fabrication", "Custom brackets, signs, panels, covers", "Field measurement and design assistance", "Galvanized steel fabrication", "Mechanical joint assembly"], "industries": ["HVAC contractors", "Mechanical contractors", "Retrofit construction", "Residential homeowners"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "One-off to production quantities", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Accepts drawings, photos, samples, or rough sketches for quoting", "Fabricates in premium galvanized steel", "Quick pickup for finished parts", "Field measurement and design assistance available", "Mechanical joints without exposed fasteners"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1993 -> db", "Headquarters Ferndale, MI -> db", "HVAC fabrication capability -> db", "Custom fabrication capability -> db", "Serves HVAC contractors -> /", "Serves homeowners -> /", "Works with galvanized steel -> /", "Accepts drawings/photos/samples -> /", "Offers field measurement -> /", "Mechanical joints without exposed fasteners -> /", "One-off to production quantities -> /", "Quick pickup -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sheet metal, cut and bent to fit your job. Custom duct, fittings, and one-off parts when the stock item will not work.", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='diversified-metal-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Diversified Plastics, Inc. was founded in 1976 by Rod Reid in his garage in Missoula, Montana, initially supplying engineered plastic wear strips to lumber and pulp mills in the surrounding area. The family-owned business is now led by Reid''s son, Brad Reid, a mechanical engineer, alongside a team of manufacturing professionals.

The company operates as a custom plastics fabrication and engineering firm, offering injection molding of UHMW-PE and other resins, cast urethane, CNC machining, thermoforming, and custom fabrication under one roof. Its MultiFab approach combines these processes to produce hybrid components. By the end of 2025, the 3.5-acre campus will encompass over 60,000 square feet of building space with four 80,000-pound silos. The shop runs injection molding machines with shot capacities from 19 to 311 ounces and delivers tens of thousands of parts annually.

Diversified Plastics serves industries including industrial wastewater treatment, mining, forest products, grain handling, car wash equipment, oil and gas, and food and beverage. Customers range from international wastewater treatment leaders to local Montana breweries. The company ships to more than 15 countries and supports OEM replacement parts, maintenance, and new product development.

